# Query functions live in `lib/services`

HTTP fetchers and React Query `queryFn` implementations belong in `lib/services/`, grouped by **runtime first**:

- `lib/services/client/<name>/` — called from client code (`"use client"` hooks, client components)
- `lib/services/server/<name>/` — called from server code (route handlers, Server Components, Server Actions)
- `lib/services/shared/<name>/` — isomorphic functions **and** contract types used on more than one runtime

`lib/query` holds query keys, cache merge/ingest, persist, and hooks that *call* those fetchers.

Each service is a folder with `index.ts`. Shared also has `types.ts` (params, function type, return type) re-exported from `index.ts`. Client and server folders are implementation-only unless the client re-exports shared types for DX.

Do not add a `lib/services` barrel. Import the service folder.

```ts
import { getDashboardData } from "@/lib/services/client/getDashboardData";
import { getDashboardData } from "@/lib/services/server/getDashboardData";
import type { SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/shared/getDashboardData";
```

## Environment markers

- Every `lib/services/server/<name>/index.ts` starts with `import "server-only"`.
- Every `lib/services/client/<name>/index.ts` starts with `import "client-only"`.
- `shared/` has neither.

Folders are for humans. These packages are the actual import guard.

## Contract types

Canonical types live in `shared/<name>/`. Never import types from `server/` (it is `server-only`; `import type` can still trip the client boundary).

- Client modules that already import the function may also import types from `client/<name>/` (the client folder re-exports shared types).
- Type-only callers (`lib/query`, UI that only needs the DTO) import from `shared/`.
- Server implementations import types from `shared/` and do **not** re-export them.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — network I/O next to cache keys
// lib/query/sprint-board.ts
export const getDashboardData = async (sprintNumber?: number) => {
  const response = await fetch("/api/sprint-board");
  return response.json();
};

// ❌ BAD — nested folder named after the function
// lib/services/client/getDashboardData/getDashboardData/index.ts

// ❌ BAD — ungrouped service (no client/server/shared)
// lib/services/getDashboardData/index.ts

// ❌ BAD — type-only caller importing from server
// import type { SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/server/getDashboardData";

// ✅ GOOD — shared contract types
// lib/services/shared/getDashboardData/types.ts
export type GetDashboardDataParams = { sprintNumber?: number };
export type SprintBoardData = { /* return type */ };
export type GetDashboardData = (
  sprintNumber?: GetDashboardDataParams["sprintNumber"],
) => Promise<SprintBoardData>;

// lib/services/shared/getDashboardData/index.ts
export type { GetDashboardData, GetDashboardDataParams, SprintBoardData } from "./types";

// lib/services/client/getDashboardData/index.ts
import "client-only";
export type { GetDashboardData, GetDashboardDataParams, SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/shared/getDashboardData";
export const getDashboardData: GetDashboardData = async (sprintNumber) => { /* HTTP */ };

// lib/services/server/getDashboardData/index.ts
import "server-only";
export const getDashboardData = async (sprintNumber?: number): Promise<SprintBoardData> => { /* Jira */ };

// lib/query/useSprintBoard.ts — client caller (function + types from client)
import { getDashboardData } from "@/lib/services/client/getDashboardData";
import type { SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/client/getDashboardData";

// lib/query/sprint-board.ts — type-only isomorphic caller
import type { SprintBoardData } from "@/lib/services/shared/getDashboardData";
```

Not every domain needs all three folders. Jira has no `client/` — the browser never talks to Jira.

```
lib/services/server/jira/     jiraFetch, credentials, fetchBoardBody, resolveSprint  + import "server-only"
lib/services/shared/jira/     SprintRef, LedgerParent, format helpers, parseSprintParam
lib/services/server/getDashboardData/  getDashboardData (calls server/jira)
```

```ts
import { fetchBoardBody, resolveSprint } from "@/lib/services/server/jira";
import { parseSprintParam, type SprintRef } from "@/lib/services/shared/jira";
```
